namespace pdg { /**

\fn Uint8Array pdg::MemBlock::getData()
\brief Copy the block's bytes into a new plain Uint8Array.

Returns the same standard JavaScript array type on desktop native, Node,
browser, and iOS runtimes. Each call copies all bytes without text decoding,
including zero and values above 127. Changing the returned array does not
change this MemBlock or arrays returned by earlier calls.

\return An independently owned Uint8Array with getDataSize() elements, or an
empty Uint8Array for an empty block. The result is not a Node Buffer;
slice() copies bytes and subarray() shares the returned array's memory.

\par Example
\code{.js}
const writer = new pdg.Serializer();
writer.serialize_1u(255);
const bytes = writer.getDataPtr().getData();
const copy = bytes.slice();
\endcode

\par Node.js Buffer conversion
Use this form when a Node.js API specifically requires a Buffer. getData()
copies the native block once; the Buffer then shares that snapshot without
another payload copy. Include the offset and length so only the array's visible
bytes are exposed, even when converting a subarray.

\note These examples require Node.js Buffer support. The shared Buffer and
Uint8Array reflect each other's mutations, but neither changes the MemBlock.

\code{.js}
const bytes = writer.getDataPtr().getData();
const buffer = Buffer.from(bytes.buffer, bytes.byteOffset, bytes.byteLength);
\endcode

\warning The shorter form below makes an additional full copy of the bytes:
one copy from native memory into the Uint8Array, then another into the Buffer.
For an N-byte block, it copies 2N bytes and needs storage for both N-byte
payloads until the temporary array can be collected. This adds copy time and
memory/garbage-collection pressure, especially for large or frequent transfers.
Use it when an independent Buffer copy is intentional.

\code{.js}
const bufferCopy = Buffer.from(writer.getDataPtr().getData());
\endcode

The removed MemBlock.toBuffer() method can be replaced by the shared-view form
above with the same single payload copy.
\see getBytes()

**/ }
